From 950f9c1e2c66ed4898cc957d48e4b9de7a4ae99c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Markus Volk <f_l_k@t-online.de>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 13:29:02 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] moc: make metatypes complete before they are registered

Several headers register Q_PROPERTY, signal or slot parameters of types
that are only forward declared at that point. Doing so instantiates Qt's
checkTypeIsSuitableForMetaType for an incomplete type, and because
template instantiations are cached per translation unit, the later
registration of the very same class inherits the negative result. gcc 16
turns this into a hard error:

  qmetatype.h: error: static assertion failed: Meta Types must be fully defined
  qml.hpp: warning: defining 'qs::service::pipewire::PwNodeIface', which
  previously failed to be complete in a SFINAE context

It only surfaces because cmake concatenates the generated moc sources of
a target into one mocs_compilation.cpp, which puts the probe and the
definition into the same translation unit.

services/pipewire: Pipewire and PwNodeLinkTracker move below the object
interfaces they refer to. wayland/toplevel and hyprland/ipc include the
header that defines the type instead of forward declaring it; neither
include is circular.

Upstream-Status: Pending

Signed-off-by: Markus Volk <f_l_k@t-online.de>
